              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "غزا — ghazā — \"to invade, to raid\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "غزا الجيش البلاد المجاورة. ghazā al-jaysh al-bilād al-mujāwira. The army invaded the neighbouring lands."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: يغزو, yaghzū."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Of space: غزو الفضاء, the conquest of space."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "غزا (ghazā) is built on the native Arabic root gh-z-w (Lane), \"to aim at, to seek\", and \"to go out to fight\"; ghazw is a raid."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
